<title>SPAIN: Spain govt may speed up Endesa sale - press.</title>
<headline>Spain govt may speed up Endesa sale - press.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish state holding firm SEPI may speed up the privatisation of Endesa, selling 40 percent of the electricity giant in the autumn rather than the 20 percent stake initially planned, local newspapers reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>SEPI chairman Pedro Ferreras said the state might consider accelerating the privatisation given the popularity of the February sale of 20.9 percent of Telefonica and the anticipated success of this month's sale of a 10.0 percent stake in Repsol.</p>
<p>No-one at SEPI was available to comment.</p>
<p>SEPI still owns approximately 67 percent of Endesa.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
